<subpara id="X39400000Y200VC_12" type-id="51" category="05" proc-id="RM0550J___0000D2300000">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<ptxt>Read the freeze frame data using SST (TaSCAN). The freeze frame data records part of the engine operating condition when the malfunction occurred, and this information is useful when troubleshooting.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="X39400000Y200VC_13" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="X39400000Y200VC_13_0009" proc-id="RM0550J___0000D2700000">
<scantool type="1"/>
<testtitle>Read DTC</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Connect SST (TaSCAN) to DLC3.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Turn the IG ON and read the DTCs following the SST (TaSCAN) screen display. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000008YS014X"/>)</ptxt>
<table>
<title>Result</title>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="3.06in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.07in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>P0013/39 is output</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>P0023/39 is output</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="X39400000Y200VC_13_0001" fin="false">A</down>
<right ref="X39400000Y200VC_13_0010" fin="false">B</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="X39400000Y200VC_13_0001" proc-id="RM0550J___0000D2400000">
<scantool type="8"/>
<testtitle>Perform TaSCAN Active Test (Exhaust VVT Linear Drive Bank 1)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Connect SST (TaSCAN) to DLC3.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>With the engine stopped, turn the IG ON.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Following the SST (TaSCAN) screen display, select [Active Test] - [Exhaust VVT Linear Drive Bank 1].</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>With the engine idling, fully advance the valve timing.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>Engine stalls or idles roughly</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="X39400000Y200VC_13_0005" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="X39400000Y200VC_13_0002" fin="false">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="X39400000Y200VC_13_0010" proc-id="RM0550J___0000D2800000">
<scantool type="8"/>
<testtitle>Perform TaSCAN Active Test (Exhaust VVT Linear Drive Bank 2)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Connect SST (TaSCAN) to DLC3.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>With the engine stopped, turn the IG ON.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Following the SST (TaSCAN) screen display, select [Active Test] - [Exhaust VVT Linear Drive Bank 2].</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>With the engine idling, fully advance the valve timing.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>Engine stalls or idles roughly</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="X39400000Y200VC_13_0005" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="X39400000Y200VC_13_0002" fin="false">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="X39400000Y200VC_13_0002" proc-id="RM0550J___0000D2500000">
<testtitle>Inspect Camshaft Timing Oil Control Valve Assembly</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Remove the camshaft timing oil control valve assembly (exhaust side).</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Resistance Inspection</ptxt>
<test2>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between the terminals.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.37in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Terminal 1 - Terminal 2</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Approx. 20°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>6.9 to 7.9Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test2>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Operation Check</ptxt>
<test2>
<ptxt>Apply battery voltage between the terminals and check that the spool valve operates.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A145883J06" width="2.775699831in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>Operates</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Check that the spool valve is not stuck.</ptxt>
</atten3>
<atten4>
<ptxt>A spool valve that does not return properly due to foreign matter such as sludge being caught may cause a slight pressure leak to the advance side, which may cause a DTC to be detected.</ptxt>
</atten4>
<table>
<title>Result</title>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="3.01in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.12in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>OK</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>RH side malfunction</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>LH side malfunction</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>C</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</test2>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="X39400000Y200VC_13_0004" fin="false">A</down>
<right ref="X39400000Y200VC_13_0006" fin="true">B</right>
<right ref="X39400000Y200VC_13_0011" fin="true">C</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="X39400000Y200VC_13_0004" proc-id="RM0550J___0000D2600000">
<testtitle>Inspect Wire Harness and Connector (Engine Control Computer - Camshaft Timing Oil Control Valve Assembly)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<ptxt>For the wire harness and connector inspection procedure and precautions, see <xref href="RM0000008YS014X" label="Seep01"/></ptxt>
</atten4>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Disconnect connector A of the engine control computer.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Disconnect the camshaft timing oil control valve assembly connector.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between the terminals. (see <xref label="Seep02" href="X39400000QV01SD"/> for Terminals of ECU)</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A154184J08" width="7.106578999in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
